# Prettier reads this from the directory it is *run* in, not from the repo
# root — so each workspace carries its own. The shared style lives in the root
# `.prettierrc.json`, which is resolved by walking up and is therefore single.
#
# `.gitignore` is honoured by default (Prettier 3), so node_modules, dist and
# the build output need no mention here.

# npm rewrites this on every install; formatting it only creates conflicts.
package-lock.json
.verification/

# Prisma owns these. `prisma format` is the tool for the schema, and a
# migration is a historical record that must not be rewritten after the fact.
libs/prisma/prisma/migrations/
libs/prisma/prisma/schema.prisma

# Build output. Prettier reads `.gitignore` from the directory it runs in too,
# and neither workspace has one — the repository's lives at the root — so the
# compiler's output has to be named here. Formatting it is meaningless, and
# *checking* it is worse: `format:check` would pass in CI (which checks before
# it builds) and fail on any machine that had run a build.
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
